From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topology: notify when an expired neighbor is removed

The topology garbage collector removed neighbors after 60 seconds without
publishing the topology-change event required by ADR-0014.  Consequently no
Topology Notification was sent and other IEEE 1905 nodes had no protocol
signal that the local neighbor view had changed.

Publish a typed NeighborExpired event after removing the node and releasing
the topology database write lock.  A dedicated consumer feeds that event into
the existing Topology Notification transmitter, preserving its multicast
format, message-ID allocation and notification-sent state transition.  If the
event receiver ever lags, send one convergence notification rather than
silently losing the topology change.

Do not publish for incomplete nodes removed from a temporary convergence
state: those nodes never became established topology neighbors.  Add a unit
test for the expiry, removal and event-publication boundary.

